    <forecast>
        <area aac="SA_FA001" description="South Australia" type="region">
            <forecast-period start-time-local="2026-09-13T09:45:47+09:30" end-time-local="2026-09-13T09:45:47+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-09-13T00:15:47Z" end-time-utc="2026-09-13T00:15:47Z">
                <text type="warning_summary_footer">For latest warnings go to www.bom.gov.au, subscribe to RSS feeds, call 1300 659 210* or listen for warnings on relevant TV and radio broadcasts.</text>
                <text type="synoptic_situation">A trough will move across SA today ahead of a high pressure ridge that will build in the wake. A cold front will then slip across southern coasts late Monday and early Tuesday, before the high moves across waters to the south to be centred over Victoria by Thursday.</text>
                <text type="product_footer">* Calls to 1300 numbers cost around 27.5c incl. GST, higher from mobiles or public phones.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
        <area aac="SA_PW006" description="Riverland" type="public-district" parent-aac="SA_FA001">
            <forecast-period index="0" start-time-local="2026-09-13T00:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-09-14T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-09-12T14:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-09-13T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. High chance of showers, becoming less likely in the late afternoon and evening. A thunderstorm likely in the late morning and afternoon. Winds north to northwesterly 25 to 35 km/h turning west to southwesterly in the early afternoon then decreasing to 15 to 25 km/h in the evening. Daytime maximum temperatures in the mid to high 20s.</text>
                <text type="uv_alert">Sun protection 9:10am to 2:50pm, UV Index predicted to reach 6 [High]</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="1" start-time-local="2026-09-14T00:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-09-15T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-09-13T14:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-09-14T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. The chance of morning fog. Light winds becoming southwesterly 15 to 20 km/h in the morning then becoming light in the late evening. Overnight temperatures falling to around 8 with daytime temperatures reaching the low 20s.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="2" start-time-local="2026-09-15T00:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-09-16T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-09-14T14:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-09-15T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. Winds southerly 20 to 30 km/h. Overnight temperatures falling to around 8 with daytime temperatures reaching around 19.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="3" start-time-local="2026-09-16T00:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-09-17T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-09-15T14:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-09-16T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. Winds south to southeasterly 15 to 25 km/h becoming light during the evening. Overnight temperatures falling to around 4 with daytime temperatures reaching around 18.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
